FIX PROMPT — Emacs configuration remediation
============================================

Source: configuration review of 2026-10-24 (Emacs 31.1, branch astra_fix).
Companion file: fix.docs — same tasks, each with the full rationale and the
goals it achieves.  Read the matching section there when a task is unclear.


HOW TO USE THIS FILE (instructions for the agent)
-------------------------------------------------

1. Read AGENTS.md first and follow it: `dk/` prefix, lexical binding,
   non-package functions in src/dk-functions.el, `dk/*` variables in
   src/dk-vars.el, global keys in src/dk-keymap.el, package-specific keys in
   that package's `use-package` form, named hook helpers instead of lambdas.
   Match the surrounding comment density and style.

2. Pick the FIRST task whose heading starts with `## [ ]`:
       grep -n '^## \[ \]' fix.prompt | head -1
   Do only that one task in this session unless the user says "continue".

3. Tasks tagged [ASK] contain a decision that belongs to the user.  Before
   writing any code, ask the listed question (AskUserQuestion, recommended
   option first), then write the answer into that task's `Decision:` line.
   If the user picks "skip", mark the task `## [-]` with the reason in
   `Result:` and move on.

4. Line numbers in tasks are hints from the review snapshot.  Earlier tasks
   may have moved code: always locate the code by its content.

5. Implement the change.  Update comments that the change makes untrue.
   If a keybinding or user-visible behaviour changes, update cheatsheet.md.
   If an external tool requirement changes, update install.md.

6. Verify (both the generic checks below and the task's own `Verify:`).
   Run batch checks in a SANDBOX COPY of the config, never in
   ~/.config/emacs itself, so history/recentf/places are not rewritten.
   Re-create the sandbox after editing files (it is a copy).

   Sandbox (use the session scratchpad directory if one exists, otherwise
   `mktemp -d`; never `rm -rf` a path built from a variable):

       SB=<fresh empty directory>
       cd ~/.config/emacs
       cp -a early-init.el init.el src themes test package-quickstart.el \
             package-quickstart.elc elpa "$SB"/
       [ -f custom.el ]     && cp -a custom.el "$SB"/
       [ -d tree-sitter ]   && cp -a tree-sitter "$SB"/

   Smoke test (must print "startup OK", inspect every warning):

       cd "$SB" && emacs --batch --init-directory="$SB" \
         --eval '(setq native-comp-jit-compilation nil)' \
         --load early-init.el --eval '(package-activate-all)' \
         --load init.el --eval '(message "startup OK")'

   ERT suite (append any new test/*.el files):

       cd "$SB" && emacs --batch --init-directory="$SB" \
         --eval '(setq native-comp-jit-compilation nil)' \
         --load early-init.el --eval '(package-activate-all)' \
         --load init.el -l ert \
         -l test/dk-functions-test.el -l test/dk-integration-test.el \
         -l test/dk-packages-test.el \
         -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit

   Byte-compile warnings (should report nothing new):

       cd "$SB" && emacs --batch --init-directory="$SB" \
         --eval '(setq native-comp-jit-compilation nil)' \
         --load early-init.el --eval '(package-activate-all)' \
         --load init.el --eval '(setq byte-compile-warnings t)' \
         --eval '(dolist (f (directory-files "src" t "\\.el\\'"'"'")) (byte-compile-file f))'

   Delete the .elc files the last command leaves in "$SB/src" (they are in
   the sandbox only).  Interactive-only behaviour (GUI keys, window layout,
   popups) cannot be fully checked in batch: say so and list the manual
   steps for the user.

7. Mark the task done: change its heading `## [ ]` to `## [x]` and fill in
   `Result:` with one or two lines (files touched, what was verified,
   anything left for manual testing).  Do not edit other tasks' status.

8. Do not commit unless the user asks.  Each task suggests a commit subject
   in the repository's imperative style.  Never commit fix.prompt/fix.docs
   changes mixed into a config commit unless the user asks.

9. Stop and report: what changed, verification output summary, manual
   checks for the user, and the ID of the next open task.


STATUS LEGEND:  [ ] open   [x] done   [-] skipped by user decision


