## [x] T01 · Fix the haskell-ts REPL command (and its false-passing test)

Files: src/dk-languages.el (~58-67), test/dk-integration-test.el (~4-14)
Problem: `:bind` creates an autoload for `dk/haskell-ts-run-repl` before
`:config` runs, so `(unless (fboundp 'dk/haskell-ts-run-repl) (defalias ...))`
never fires.  C-c C-z / C-c C-r in haskell-ts-mode signal "Autoloading file
.../haskell-ts-mode.elc failed to define function dk/haskell-ts-run-repl".
Change:
  - Define the alias when the symbol is unbound OR still an autoload:
      (unless (and (fboundp 'dk/haskell-ts-run-repl)
                   (not (autoloadp (symbol-function 'dk/haskell-ts-run-repl))))
        (defalias ...))
    Keep the existing intent: once a real function is captured, a reload of
    dk-languages after inf-haskell is loaded must not replace it.
  - Update the comment to say why the autoload case must be handled.
  - Strengthen the integration test: after `(require 'haskell-ts-mode)` assert
    `(functionp (symbol-function 'dk/haskell-ts-run-repl))` and
    `(not (autoloadp (symbol-function 'dk/haskell-ts-run-repl)))`, both before
    and after `(require 'inf-haskell)` and the `(load "dk-languages" nil t)`.
Verify: ERT passes; in batch after `(require 'haskell-ts-mode)`,
`(autoloadp (symbol-function 'dk/haskell-ts-run-repl))` is nil.  Revert the
fix temporarily (mentally or in the sandbox) to confirm the new test fails
without it.
Commit: "Fix haskell-ts REPL alias shadowed by its autoload"
Result: src/dk-languages.el (alias also defined while the symbol is still an
autoload), test/dk-integration-test.el (asserts a real, non-autoload function
before/after inf-haskell and reload).  New test fails on the old code, passes now.


## [x] T02 · Stop splitting Cargo/cabal/Go workspaces into per-package projects

Files: src/dk-navigation.el (~63-67)
Problem: `project-vc-extra-root-markers` contains "Cargo.toml", "*.cabal" and
"go.mod"; the nearest marker wins, so every workspace member becomes its own
project and Eglot starts one LSP server per member.
Change:
  - Replace per-package markers with workspace-level ones:
      '("cabal.project" "stack.yaml" "Cargo.lock" "go.work"
        "compile_commands.json")
  - Rewrite the comment above it: markers exist to give NON-git directories a
    root; inside git the repository root (or a workspace file) is the root,
    because Eglot uses the project root as the server root.  Mention the
    trade-off (a lone crate outside git becomes a project after its first
    build creates Cargo.lock; a lone cabal package outside git needs a
    cabal.project).
Verify: in a scratch git repo with Cargo.toml at the top and crates/a,
crates/b each containing Cargo.toml + src/lib.rs, `(project-root
(project-current nil "<repo>/crates/a/src/"))` returns the repo root (it
returned crates/a/ before the change).  Smoke test + ERT pass.
Commit: "Root projects at workspace level, not per package"
Result: src/dk-navigation.el markers + comments.  Scratch cargo workspace: root from
crates/a/src is now the repo root (was crates/a/).  Smoke + ERT pass.


## [x] T03 · Stop hiding git-tracked files with the ignored-directory list

Files: src/dk-vars.el (~48-79), src/dk-navigation.el (~68-80, ~98-107),
       src/dk-completion.el (~147-159)
Problem: `dk/project-ignored-directories` excludes any directory named
build, dist, vendor (…) at any depth from C-x p f, rgrep and consult-ripgrep,
even when git tracks it (verified: tracked build/tool.sh vanished from
`project-files`).  ripgrep's `--glob=!NAME` also excludes plain FILES of
that name.
Change:
  - Remove the ambiguous generic names "build", "dist" and "vendor" from the
    list.  Keep names that are unambiguously generated: "dist-newstyle"
    ".stack-work" ".hie" "target" "cmake-build-*" ".cache" "node_modules"
    ".direnv".
  - Make the ripgrep globs directory-only: format them as
    `--glob=!%s/` (gitignore semantics: trailing slash = directories only).
  - Update the dk-vars.el docstring: what the list is for, why generic names
    are excluded, and that a project needing more can set
    `project-vc-ignores` in its own .dir-locals.el (the variable is
    `safe-local-variable` for lists).
Verify: in a scratch git repo with tracked build/tool.sh, `project-files`
includes it.  In a scratch dir containing target/x.txt (directory) and a
file literally named `target`, run rg with the resulting
`consult-ripgrep-args` globs: target/x.txt is skipped, the file `target` is
searched.  Smoke test + ERT pass.
Commit: "Narrow ignored build directories to generated ones"
Result: src/dk-vars.el (list + docstring), src/dk-completion.el (`--glob=!%s/`),
cheatsheet.md.  Tracked build/tool.sh now in project-files; rg skips target/x.txt
but searches a file named `target`.  Smoke + ERT pass.


## [x] T04 · Make ESC stop deleting other windows

Files: src/dk-functions.el, src/dk-keymap.el (~10-12)
Problem: `<escape>` runs `keyboard-escape-quit`, which calls
`delete-other-windows` when there is nothing else to cancel (verified: 2
windows -> 1).  The comment claims it works "like C-g".
Change:
  - Keep `<escape>` bound to `keyboard-escape-quit` (so corfu's
    `[remap keyboard-escape-quit]` keeps working) and add a named :around
    advice in dk-functions.el:
      (defun dk/escape-quit-keep-windows (orig-fun &rest args)
        "Run ORIG-FUN (`keyboard-escape-quit') without deleting windows."
        (cl-letf (((symbol-function 'one-window-p) #'always))
          (apply orig-fun args)))
    `(require 'cl-lib)` at the top of dk-functions.el if not present.
  - Install it in dk-keymap.el next to the binding with `advice-add`
    (idempotent on reload).  Fix the comment: ESC now cancels the region,
    prefix argument, minibuffer and recursive edit, but never touches the
    window layout.
Verify (batch): split window, call `keyboard-escape-quit` -> still 2
windows; with an active region, ESC deactivates it.  Manual (GUI): ESC in a
minibuffer aborts it; ESC with a corfu popup closes the popup; ESC ESC ESC
also keeps windows.
Commit: "Keep window layout when ESC quits"
Result: src/dk-functions.el (cl-lib, dk/escape-quit-keep-windows), src/dk-keymap.el,
cheatsheet.md.  Batch: 2 windows kept, region deactivated, advice single after
reload.  Manual: ESC in minibuffer, with corfu popup, ESC ESC ESC.


## [x] T05 · Make helpful reuse its window and let q close it

Files: src/dk-functions.el (~55-72), src/dk-ui.el (~111-121)
Problem: `dk/helpful-open` splits on every call, including following links
inside a helpful buffer (verified: 2 lookups -> 3 windows).  The window is
filled with `set-window-buffer`, so it has no quit-restore parameter and
`q` cannot delete it.
Change: rewrite `dk/helpful-open` around `display-buffer`:
  - In a helpful buffer: `(pop-to-buffer-same-window buf)` (link navigation
    replaces the content in place).
  - Elsewhere:
      (display-buffer
       buf `((display-buffer-reuse-mode-window
              display-buffer-in-direction
              display-buffer-same-window)
             (mode . helpful-mode)
             (direction . ,(if (window-full-width-p) 'right 'below))))
    i.e. reuse a visible helpful window, otherwise split right/below as
    before, otherwise use the current window.  Point stays in the original
    window when a split is made (display-buffer does not select).
  - Update the docstring and the dk-ui.el comment.
Verify (batch, count `window-list`): from a code buffer -> 2 windows; call
again from the helpful window -> still 2; call again from the code window
-> still 2 (reused); `quit-window` in the helpful window -> 1 window.
Manual: C-h f, follow a link, press q.
Commit: "Reuse the helpful window and let q close it"
Result: src/dk-functions.el, src/dk-ui.el.  Batch: 2/2/2 windows.  Emacs 31 quit-restore
makes q step back through the buffers the window showed, then delete it (q x4 ->
1 window after car/cdr/cons/list), not on the first q.  Manual: C-h f, link, q.


