## [x] T07 · Stop apheleia from reformatting Haskell and Elisp unasked  [ASK]

Files: src/dk-functions.el (~174-185), src/dk-programming.el (~117-127),
       src/dk-languages.el (comments mentioning dk/no-clang-format-p)
Problem: `apheleia-mode-alist` maps haskell-mode/haskell-ts-mode to
fourmolu and emacs-lisp-mode to lisp-indent, so saving re-formats whole
files in projects that use another style (or none).  C/C++ is already gated
on a .clang-format file; Haskell and Elisp are not.
Question: "How should format-on-save treat Haskell and Emacs Lisp?"
  1. (Recommended) Haskell only when fourmolu.yaml exists in the tree;
     never for Emacs Lisp.
  2. Never for either.
  3. Keep formatting both (skip this task).
Decision: option 1 — Haskell only with fourmolu.yaml; never Emacs Lisp.
Change (for option 1; adapt for 2):
  - Replace `dk/no-clang-format-p` with `dk/apheleia-inhibit-p` in
    dk-functions.el: non-nil when (a) C/C++ (ts and classic) without
    .clang-format/_clang-format, (b) haskell-mode/haskell-ts-mode without
    fourmolu.yaml in a dominating directory, (c) `lisp-data-mode` derived
    buffers (covers emacs-lisp-mode, lisp-interaction-mode).  Docstring
    explains each clause.
  - Register it in `apheleia-inhibit-functions`; on reload remove the old
    symbol from that list too (`(remove-hook 'apheleia-inhibit-functions
    #'dk/no-clang-format-p)` style, it is a plain list: use `delq`).
  - Update comments in dk-programming.el and dk-languages.el.
Verify: in temp buffers: c-ts-mode without config -> inhibit non-nil;
haskell-mode in a dir without fourmolu.yaml -> non-nil, with one -> nil;
emacs-lisp-mode -> non-nil; go-ts-mode -> nil.  ERT + smoke test pass.
Commit: "Format Haskell and Elisp only when a project opts in"
Result: src/dk-functions.el (dk/apheleia-inhibit-p replaces dk/no-clang-format-p),
src/dk-programming.el, src/dk-languages.el, install.md, cheatsheet.md.  All
temp-buffer cases as specified; old symbol removed on reload.  Smoke + ERT pass.


