## [x] T14 · Make Go indentation width consistent with gofmt's tabs

Files: src/dk-functions.el, src/dk-languages.el (~126-137)
Problem: `go-ts-mode-indent-offset 4` is the indent step, not the tab
display width (the comment is wrong).  `tab-width` stays 8 with
`indent-tabs-mode t`, so typed lines get 4 spaces, gofmt rewrites them as
tabs shown 8 wide, and indentation jumps after each save.
Change:
  - Add `dk/go-ts-tab-width` (dk-functions.el): `(setq-local tab-width
    go-ts-mode-indent-offset)`.
  - `:hook (go-ts-mode . dk/go-ts-tab-width)` in the go-ts-mode form.
  - Correct the comment: offset = indent step, tab-width set to match so one
    level = one tab displayed 4 wide; gofmt output unaffected.
Verify: in a temp buffer `(go-ts-mode)` (needs the go grammar; otherwise
call the hook function directly in a buffer with indent-tabs-mode t) ->
`tab-width` 4.
Commit: "Display Go tabs at the configured indent width"
Result: src/dk-functions.el (`dk/go-ts-tab-width`), src/dk-languages.el.  Hook
function -> tab-width 4; on go-ts-mode-hook.  go-ts-mode itself not run (no grammar).


