Files: src/dk-defaults.el
Problem: `indent-tabs-mode` is never set (default t), so lines typed in C,
Elisp and other modes mix tabs and spaces at >= 8 columns.
Change: `(setq-default indent-tabs-mode nil)` in dk-defaults.el with a
comment: modes whose formats need tabs (go-ts-mode, makefile modes) set it
back buffer-locally; per-project tab conventions belong in .dir-locals.el.
Verify: default value nil; in temp buffers `(makefile-mode)` -> t,
`(go-ts-mode)` -> t (or confirm in Emacs source that go-ts-mode sets
`indent-tabs-mode` locally), `(c-ts-mode)`/`(emacs-lisp-mode)` -> nil.
Commit: "Indent with spaces by default"
Result: src/dk-defaults.el, cheatsheet.md.  Default nil; makefile t; elisp/c nil.
go-ts-mode sets indent-tabs-mode t locally (go-ts-mode.el:339), not run: no grammar.


## [x] T16 · Keep M-o = other-window inside ibuffer

Files: src/dk-navigation.el (or dk-ui.el), cheatsheet.md
Problem: `ibuffer-mode-map` binds M-o to `ibuffer-visit-buffer-1-window`,
so window switching stops in exactly the buffer C-x C-b opens.
Change: `(use-package ibuffer :ensure nil :bind (:map ibuffer-mode-map
("M-o" . other-window)))` with a comment; the shadowed command stays on
M-x / the menu.
Verify: after `(require 'ibuffer)`, `(keymap-lookup ibuffer-mode-map
"M-o")` is `other-window`.
Commit: "Keep M-o as other-window in ibuffer"
Result: src/dk-navigation.el (ibuffer use-package), cheatsheet.md.  ibuffer-mode-map
M-o = other-window.  Manual: C-x C-b, M-o switches window without deleting others.


## [x] T17 · Move mc/mark-all-like-this off the major-mode key C-c ;  [ASK]

Files: src/dk-defaults.el (~106-110), cheatsheet.md
Problem: `C-c ;` is reserved for major modes by Emacs key conventions; org
binds it to `org-toggle-comment`, so mark-all is unavailable in org.
Question: "Which key should mc/mark-all-like-this use?"
  1. (Recommended) C-c A
  2. C-c a
  3. Keep C-c ; (skip)
Decision: option 1 — C-c A.
Change: rebind in the multiple-cursors `:bind`, add a comment about the
convention.
Verify: global binding of the new key; `C-c ;` in org-mode-map still
`org-toggle-comment`.
Commit: "Move mark-all-like-this to a user key"
Result: src/dk-defaults.el, cheatsheet.md.  Global C-c A = mc/mark-all-like-this, C-c ;
globally nil, org-mode-map C-c ; still org-toggle-comment.


## [x] T18 · Make C-c e (eval-buffer) Elisp-only

Files: src/dk-keymap.el (~47), src/dk-programming.el, cheatsheet.md
Problem: `C-c e` evaluates any buffer as Lisp — Markdown, C, shell files.
Change: remove the global binding; add `(use-package elisp-mode :ensure nil
:bind (:map emacs-lisp-mode-map ("C-c e" . eval-buffer)))` in
dk-programming.el.  Check whether `lisp-interaction-mode-map` inherits from
