## [x] T27 · Clean recentf and save it periodically under the daemon

Files: src/dk-vars.el, src/dk-navigation.el (~13-21)
Problem: no `recentf-exclude`, so elpa sources, COMMIT_EDITMSG, /tmp files
and backup/autosave files fill C-x C-r; under the systemd daemon recentf is
only written on a clean exit, so a crash loses the session's list.
Change:
  - `recentf-exclude` in `:custom`: regexps for the elpa directory
    (`package-user-dir`), `dk/backup-directory`, `dk/auto-save-directory`,
    `temporary-file-directory`, and "/COMMIT_EDITMSG\\'"
    (use `regexp-quote` on directory names).
  - A periodic save: `dk/recentf-save-timer` (defvar in dk-vars.el) holding
    `(run-with-idle-timer 300 t #'dk/recentf-save-quietly)`; cancel an
    existing timer first so reloading the module does not stack timers.
    `dk/recentf-save-quietly` (dk-functions.el) calls `recentf-save-list`
    with `inhibit-message` bound to t.
Verify: `recentf-exclude` value; `(recentf-include-p
"<elpa>/foo/foo.el")` nil, ordinary file t; reloading dk-navigation twice
leaves exactly one timer (`timer-idle-list`).
Commit: "Exclude noise from recentf and save it periodically"
Result: src/dk-vars.el (`dk/recentf-save-timer'), src/dk-functions.el
(`dk/recentf-directory-regexp' matches both ~/ and expanded names,
`dk/recentf-save-quietly'), src/dk-navigation.el, cheatsheet.md.  elpa, /tmp and
COMMIT_EDITMSG excluded, ordinary file kept; one timer after reloading twice.


